<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37408" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξῐσ-όω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>make equal</i> or <i>even, bring to a level with,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί τινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OT</u>
					425
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηδ᾽ ἐξισώσῃς τάσδε τοῖς ἐμοῖς
				κακοῖς</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				1507
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τοῖς μεγίστοις ἐγκλήμασι τὸ πρᾶγμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antipho
					4.2.1
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ζυγά</span>
			<i>bring</i> the teams <i>abreast,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				738
			</span></i>:—
				Med.
			, <i>make oneself equal,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δράκοντι μῆκος ἐξισουμένην σαύραν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Babr.
					41.2
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be</i> or <i>become equal,</i> c. dat., <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.34
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				6.111
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				563a
			</span></i>, etc.; <i>to be reduced to a level with,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					8.13
				</span></i>
			; <i>to be a match for, rival,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.97
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				2.52
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός τινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Agis</u>
					7
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>put on a level,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς πολίτας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ra.</u>
					688
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				4.91
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mu.</u>
				397a8
			</span></i> (
				Pass.
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φύλοπις οὐκέτ᾽
			ἐξισοῦται</span> is <i>levelled, equalized,</i> i.e.
				<i>resolved in harmony,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				1072
			</span></i> (lyr.); lit., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξισωθέντος τοῦ μέχρι τῶν τειχῶν
					διαστήματος</span>”
				<i>levelled,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>BJ</u>
					5.3.5
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> intr., <i>to
				be equal</i> or <i>like,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μητρὶ δ᾽ οὐδὲν ἐξισοῖ</span>
			<i>acts</i> in no way <i>like</i> a mother, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				1194
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τοῖς ἄλλοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					6.87
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τισί</span>
			<i>make</i> a line of battle <i>equal</i> to the enemy's, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				5.71
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
